	"name": "Bullet Hell",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/weapons/ammunition/bullets-cartridge-shell-gray.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>At 17th level, your mastery of Gun-fu is unparalleled. You wield light firearms as extensions of your own body, and no example of Gun-fu will ever be as encapsulating of that fact as the unleashing of Bullet Hell.  As an action, expend 3 exertion and make an attack roll with advantage. Ignoring cover, including total cover of 1 inch or less of stone or up to 4 inches of wood, compare your attack roll to the AC of any number of hostile creatures of your choosing within your light firearm's normal range. On a hit, they take damage as if you shot them with your light firearm.</p><p>Should you critically hit, each target must make a Wisdom save or be stunned until the start of your next turn.</p>",
